# A never-assigned name in a NUMERIC slot is INFO, not an error: numi() reads
# null as 0, so the statement runs with 0 instead of failing.  This pins the
# severity split introduced when the two undefined-var rules were merged
# (ref m07644): num/bool slot -> INFO, any other slot -> ERR.
set t 0
op add t zz 1
print t
end
